### This is the README file for the CCT_Matlab_PPC subfolder from the HDDM_Vero project.
### This subfodler is a copy of Dr Chih-Chung Tings simulation code.

Here, I am specifying the purpose and structure of files & folders:

### data: 
- holds the csv file "GarciaParticipants_Eye_Response_Feed_Allfix_addm_OV_Abs_CCT" which is the main csv file for analysis
- holds matlab files that contain most columns of interest of the transformed csv file (transformed into mat files to fit Chih-Chung Tings simulation code)


### These files below are directly taken from Dr Chih-Chung Ting and serve as orientation

- EvidenceAccumulate_Bright.m
- Sim_Bright_fixedALL.m
- Sim_Bright_HDDMestimate.m
- Figure_Accuracy_RT.m --> plots accuracy and RT from the empirical data with the overlayed simulation


### These files below are from Prof Dr Sebastian Gluth ( modified to plot RT and gaze data from the csv file but also to plot the .mat simulations)

- simulationESmodel_v2.m   --> Sebastian's original simulation idea
- plotEmpiricalData.m       --> this file plots not only the emprical data (csv file) but also plots dwell-time, gaze, RT & accuracy plots from the simulations
- simulationESmodel_plotWithSEM.m   --> holds plotting functions


### These files below are used in my project to simulate data with paramters from the aDDM and DDM 

### Code for the aDDM can be used with or wihtout starting point bias
- EvidenceAccumulate_ES_VAL_m2.m
- gelman_rubin_ES_VAL_m7.csv
- params_ES_VAL_m7.csv 
- Sim_ES_fixedALL_VAL_7.m

### code for the dual addm with different attentional/inattentional weights for E & S options (this is flawed and probably not correct yet)
- EvidenceAccumulate_ES_m45.m
- gelman_rubin_ES_m45.m
- params_ES_m45.m
- Sim_ES_m45_fixedALL.m

### This code computes mean and STD per subject and per OV level, then lognormal transforms them similar to Ting & Gluth, 2024 style but I think it has some issues as I am unsure about the correctness of the lognormal transformation

- Fixation_Metrics_Simulation.m
- Fixation_mean_log_simulation_ES

Models that belong to the parameter files:

## E is the upper boundary for the models below
#### params_ES_ZBIAS_m25
 - here we include z in include list
    v_reg = {'model': 'v ~ 1 + ES_AttentionW + ES_InattentionW', 'link_func': lambda x: x}
    reg_descr = [v_reg]

#### params_ES_ZBIAS_m26
-  z is 0.5 and not a free parameter, not included in the include_list
    v_reg = {'model': 'v ~ 1 + ES_AttentionW + ES_InattentionW', 'link_func': lambda x: x}
    reg_descr = [v_reg]

#### params_ES_VAL_m7
- no intercept (z is inlcuded as free param)
    v_reg = {'model': 'v ~ 0 + ES_AttentionW + ES_InattentionW', 'link_func': lambda x: x}
    reg_descr = [v_reg]

## Correct (1) is the upper boundary for the models below - accuracy coded

#### params_ES_m45
- z is fixed at 0.5 not inclded as a free parameter
v_reg = {'model': 'v ~ 1 + AttentionW_E + AttentionW_S + InattentionW_E + InattentionW_S', 'link_func': lambda x: x}
    reg_descr = [v_reg]
    depends_on = {'a': 'OVcate'} 